# Feature Pull Requests

## Merge Policy

- Feature work merges via PR when publishing; do not push to protected trunk without review.
- **One PR per verified phase** as a GitHub stacked PR when the user asks to push.
- Prefer `gh stack` when available; otherwise manual `--base` stacking.
- Small fixes with no SDD may use a single PR; use `N/A` for SDD/ADR sections.
- **Do not push** unless the user explicitly asks.

## Branch rules

- Branch: `<feature-slug>/phase-<n>`
- Title: `[<feature-slug>] Phase N: <phase title>`

## Required PR Description Sections

```markdown
## 0. Tracking

- SDD: `docs/sdd/<feature-slug>.md`
- Stack: phase N of M (GitHub stacked PR)
- Stack tool: `gh stack` / manual fallback
- PR base branch:
- Phase branch:

## 1. Deployment prerequisites

### Config changes
### Database changes
### Redis changes
### Deploy order

## 2. Changes summary

### Feature overview
### SDD
### ADRs

## 3. Verification

### Tests
### Test coverage
### Linting and static checks

## 4. Instrumentation and production verification

### Instrumentation added or changed
### How to verify in production
```

Fill every subsection; use `None` / `N/A` when not applicable. Never invent test/coverage results.
